# Protonation sites: CREST finds the protomers, xTB and DFT refine the lowest one.
recipe: protonation-sites
title: Protonation sites
field: Conformations
summary: CREST protonation sites, then xTB, then DFT optimisation and frequencies of the lowest protomer
description: CREST finds the protonation sites and ranks the protomers, xTB re-optimises the lowest and a DFT optimisation with frequencies refines it. The steps after CREST get the charge of the structure plus one. The product is a cation, so the rule that adds diffuse functions for anions is left out.
role: dft | DFT optimisation and frequencies | B3LYP | 6-31+G(d) | the usual starting level; diffuse functions when the molecule is an anion
rules: heavy-ecp, size, registered

variant: orca | CREST, xTB, ORCA | ORCA
